| ShortSummary    = [[Jeff Probst]] welcomes the 21 new castaways to ''Survivor'' and reveals that they will be playing with "Permanent Uncertainty." The castaways are then marooned together on one beach with limited supplies and no set tribal lines. The players discover a sign informing them that not everyone will start the game together, as they must agree on one person to begin the game on their own. Lewis volunteers to go on the journey.

*'''Journey:''' Lewis goes on a journey and is sent to Exile Island. On Day 2, he must chop down a thick mast within a set time limit to claim the Hidden Immunity Idol at the top. However, Lewis fails to chop down the mast before time runs out and is unsuccessful in earning the idol.

Back on the beach, a helicopter arrives. Aaliyah, Devin, Jelly and Ori solidify their alliance with Sharonda as the fifth member. The helicopter drops off a bag containing their tribe buffs, revealing the new tribe divisions: Savu consisting of Alexis, Ana, Carter, Cristian, Eric, Kristin, Linnea, Ori, Rob and Sharonda, and Toka consisting of Aaliyah, Brady, Devin, Jelly, Jenna, Kilby, Maggie, Mike, Patt and Thien An.

*'''Supply Challenge:''' Each tribe must nominate one member to negotiate with the other tribe for supplies. Kristin and Kilby are selected from their respective tribe and agree to split the supplies, with Savu taking the flint, pot, machete and fishing gear, while Toka takes the camping supplies. 

At Toka, Jenna struggles to open up to her tribemates. Devin, Aaliyah and Jelly reconnect, solidifying their Helicopter Alliance. Devin and Brady grow closer and discuss targeting Jenna as the first boot. Devin also spreads around camp that Jenna may be lying about her profession.

On the Savu beach, Ori and Sharonda solidify the second half of the Helicopter Alliance, hoping to keep their connection a secret. Eric begins to rub his fellow tribemates the wrong way, which Rob takes advantage of by painting a bigger target on him. The next morning, Rob finds a Hidden Immunity Idol.

Before the Immunity Challenge, Probst welcomes the castaways to the "Open Era," explaining that anything from past ''Survivor'' seasons could be brought into play. The castaways are informed that the coin flip from ''[[Survivor 50: In the Hands of the Fans]]'' is back in play. The coin flip could increase the prize pot to $2,000,000 or eliminate the player who chooses to flip the coin. If the player is eliminated, the money rolls over to the subsequent season.

* '''Immunity Challenge:''' Tribes must race through intersecting obstacles to untie five bags containing balls. Once they retrieve all five balls, they must push them through a vertical chute to release a key. Players then use the key to unlock six heavy crates and push them underneath a cargo net to create a staircase. After all tribe members climb the staircase, two players must assemble a logo puzzle to win immunity.

Savu wins immunity, sending Toka to the first Tribal Council. Devin continues to target Jenna, while some players believe Aaliyah should be the target after she allowed the tribe to fall behind during the challenge. Patt informs Jenna that she could be the one going home, prompting Jenna to throw Aaliyah under the bus to Brady. Brady and Devin disagree over who to vote for.

At Tribal Council, Jenna admits that she struggled to open up during the first few days. Devin boldly reveals that he is voting for Jenna, causing the tribe to whisper and scramble to figure out where to vote. Aaliyah is shocked to hear that her name is also being considered. Both Jenna and Aaliyah play their Shots in the Dark, but are both "Not Safe." Aaliyah is voted out in a 6–2 vote over Jenna.
| LineColor       = #04A9E5
}}
