==Production==
Ahead of the season 50 premiere, CBS renewed ''Survivor'' for its 51st season on January 22, 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |last=White |first=Peter |date=2026-01-22 |title='Survivor' & 'The Amazing Race' Renewed At CBS |url=https://deadline.com/2026/01/survivor-the-amazing-race-renewed-cbs-1236693430/ |access-date=2026-03-21 |website=Deadline |language=en-US}}</ref> A trailer was played at the ''[[Survivor 50: In the Hands of the Fans]]'' reunion, revealing that there will be two starting tribes, a first since ''[[Survivor: Winners at War|Winners at War]]''.<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oSUzmg4zoLk |title=Survivor 51 {{!}} Sneak Peek |date=2026-05-20 |last=SurvivorOnCBS |access-date=2026-05-23 |via=YouTube}}</ref> 

Host [[Jeff Probst]] declared ''Survivor 51'' to be the beginning of "the open era", meaning that "anything that's ever happened on ''Survivor''" in past seasons, including twists and advantages, "can happen again — at any time, in any order, without warning."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Boyle |first=Kelli |date=2026-08-26 |title='Survivor 51' Cast: Meet the 21 'Open Era' Castaways |url=https://www.tvinsider.com/gallery/survivor-51-cast-open-era/ |access-date=2026-08-31 |website=TV Insider |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{Cite web |last=Terrones |first=Terry |date=2026-08-26 |title=‘Survivor 51’: Meet the 21 Castaways on Game-Changing New Season |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-features/survivor-51-new-season-cast-1236681438/ |access-date=2026-08-31 |website=The Hollywood Reporter |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-09-09 |title=Survivor Season 51 Trailer: Jeff Probst Teases a New Era with ‘Every Twist’ in Play (Exclusive) |url=https://people.com/survivor-season-51-trailer-jeff-probst-new-era-12111574 |access-date=2026-09-12 |website=People}}</ref>

